  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

  SignPath artifact configuration "installer" (docs/code-signing.md): the
  installer that make-release.ps1 makes from the signed package, as the
  release job of .github/workflows/build-windows.yml uploads it (a GitHub
  artifact, so a zip with vlc-redesign-<version>-<platform>-setup.exe at its
  root; <platform> is win64 or winarm64, the job's matrix). Inno Setup writes
  its version resource from the .iss: product name "VLC Redesign" (AppName),
  product version <version> (AppVersion), each followed by spaces, which
  make-release.ps1 trims (installer/trim-version-info.py): SignPath compares
  both values exactly. No description on <authenticode-sign>: SignPath
  Foundation's plan writes it itself.

  Paste it into the SignPath project as the artifact configuration with the
  slug "installer".
-->
<artifact-configuration xmlns="http://signpath.io/artifact-configuration/v1">
  <parameters>
    <parameter name="version" required="true" />
    <parameter name="platform" required="true" />
  </parameters>
  <zip-file>
    <pe-file path="vlc-redesign-${version}-${platform}-setup.exe" product-name="VLC Redesign" product-version="${version}">
      <authenticode-sign />
    </pe-file>
  </zip-file>
</artifact-configuration>
